                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "As these values are specified by the DMTF I don't have any strong concern with adding them without an existing user.\n\nThe \"existing user\" request is for when the implementation (libpldm) has to make its own creative choices in order to implement the specification - things like struct content and layout, function names, parameters and return values, or interactions between members of a set of APIs (e.g. the firmware update package parser or the transport APIs). These areas tend to be where we make mistakes that effect correctness and ergonomics for the library user."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This isn't super informative? Compare to the above entries.\n\nAlso `state-set` vs `stateset`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "> This isn't super informative? Compare to the above entries.\n\nWhould you prefer if I write all the 9 new enums here to make it more explicit? I just thought this would overcomplicate the description.\n\n> Also state-set vs stateset?\n\nThere is a general `enum pldm_state_set_ids` (https://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/main/include/libpldm/state_set.h#L11) and detailed state set values like `enum pldm_state_set_health_state_values`/`enum pldm_state_set_availability_values`/... (https://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/main/include/libpldm/state_set.h#L148)\n\nFrom the git log history it looked to me that the first one is referenced as `stateset` in libpldm, and the second one as `state-set`. If this is not the case I can correct the description as necessary."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Whould you prefer if I write all the 9 new enums here to make it more \n\nexplicit? I just thought this would overcomplicate the description.\n\nI'd prefer if you did list them explicitly. The idea of the changelog is that users aren't forced to read the git history.\n\nOn the second point, let's go with `state-set` and try to keep it consistent going forwards."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
